'''Mote de queso''' is a [[Colombian cuisine|Colombian]] soup dish.<ref>[http://www.caribenet.com/cartagena/index.php?name=Sections&req=viewarticle&artid=94 Caribe.net - "La Mulata"] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110708120955/http://www.caribenet.com/cartagena/index.php?name=Sections&req=viewarticle&artid=94 |date=2011-07-08 }}</ref> It is originally from the country's Atlantic coast and is made with ''ñame'' (yam) and Costeño cheese.<ref>
It has few variations in its preparation but it has garlic, coconut milk and white onions. [https://www.mycolombianrecipes.com/mote-de-queso-colombian-cheese-and-yam-soup Mote de Queso, Colombian cheese and yam soup] My Colombian Recipes</ref> It is eaten in the Caribbean area of Colombia and is a traditional dish of [[Corozal, Sucre]], Colombia.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Colombian Specialities and Dishes - Colombia|url=http://www.angloinfo.com/how-to/colombia/lifestyle/food-drink/colombian-dishes|access-date=2021-03-18|website=Angloinfo|language=en}}</ref>
